Usage: runcon CONTEXT COMMAND [ARG]...
  or:  runcon [-c] [-u USER] [-r ROLE] [-t TYPE] [-l RANGE] [COMMAND [ARG]...]

Run a program in a different SELinux security context.

WinuxCmd accepts the GNU-compatible command line surface for runcon, but
Windows does not provide SELinux process contexts. This command therefore
acts as a compatibility command and reports that the operation is not
supported on Windows.

OPTIONS:
  -c, --compute    compute process transition context before modifying
  -u, --user ARG   set user component of the context
  -r, --role ARG   set role component of the context
  -t, --type ARG   set type component of the context
  -l, --range ARG  set range component of the context
      --help       display this help and exit
  -V, --version    output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
